& [PreservedUserIntent]
  + [verbatim] "Cantor will do 3 different levels of compiling, compiling external binaries, compiling llama.cpp internal addons, and compiling attention patterns and procedures"
  + [interpretation] Slice5 activates the external-binary domain as a conventional native artifact candidate and does not treat semantic compilation as a substitute for the identified native toolchain

& [Purpose]
  + compile one exact NativeArtifact CandidateCompilationPlan and TypedSopIr into a deterministic conventional build candidate
  + begin with a Rust CLI Cargo target because the workspace already provides a locked concrete example
  + retain language source build toolchain dependency target interface capability verification signing packaging rollback and non-authority identities

& [LifecycleSeparation]
  + source authorship selects or generates candidate source without build authority
  + semantic projection binds typed SOP meaning to candidate source and build intent
  + sandboxed build later invokes an exact external compiler linker and dependency lock
  + artifact verification later checks reproducibility interface behavior capability ceiling and source correspondence
  + signing admission packaging installation deployment and execution remain independent later authorities

& [NativeArtifactCandidate]
  + binds seed plan IR source correspondence unresolved and fixed non-authority
  + binds artifact kind CLI language Rust edition crate package binary target and interface profiles
  + binds exact source file identities digests and generated-versus-selected provenance
  + binds workspace manifest package manifest dependency lock toolchain channel compiler version Cargo version target triple build profile feature set and environment policy
  + binds expected output logical identity and path policy without claiming an output digest before build
  + binds build inputs command schema finite time process memory output and artifact count limits expected receipts verification refs rollback and cleanup
  + binds declared future runtime capability requirements separately from compiler projection capabilities

& [CompilationBoundary]
  + candidate projection is pure and permits semantic_read and source_read only
  + no source generation filesystem write Cargo rustc linker build script process network dependency fetch package signing installation or execution occurs
  + Build FileWrite ProcessExecute Install Network and ExternalEffect compiler capabilities refuse in the pure candidate slice
  + actual sandbox build requires a later capability receipt and create-new output scope

& [Reproducibility]
  + dependency resolution must use the exact lockfile and offline or vendored policy unless separately authorized
  + toolchain executable identities versions target and configuration are inputs to the build receipt
  + equal admitted inputs should produce equal artifacts where the target toolchain supports reproducibility otherwise the limitation remains explicit
  + output digest exists only in a post-build artifact receipt and never as an invented pre-build value

& [Acceptance]
  + equal complete inputs yield byte-identical native candidate and digest
  + backend source manifest lock toolchain target feature profile command bound capability output path verification rollback and non-authority substitutions fail closed
  + current Cargo workspace CLI source lock and behavior remain unchanged
  + focused debug release workspace lint format evidence and diff gates pass before closure

& [LaterTargets]
  + C C++ service library and HDL or FPGA candidates reuse the semantic front end but require distinct language toolchain artifact interface verification and deployment profiles
  + no language backend may borrow another backend's artifact receipt or execution authority

& [Locked]
  + source generation filesystem mutation Cargo rustc linker build script subprocess dependency fetch signing verification admission packaging installation deployment execution internal llama.cpp modification FPGA synthesis OneDrive EVO-X2 and Minecraft
